<p>On the basis of exchange rates from 19-24 March the average RMG for sterling is above +5 per cent at 6.059 per cent. Therefore the UK green rate is currently forecast to revalue on 29 March 1997, to 0.744185, by halving its average RMG. The average RMG for the Irish punt is also over +5 per cent at 5.412 per cent. It is therefore also forecast to revalue on 29 March 1997 to 0.756530, by halving its average RMG. Since on the basis of exchange rates from 19-24 March there are no currencies with an average RMG of over +3 per cent (once the UK and Irish average RMGs have been halved) the negative threshold for devaluations is -2 per cent. Therefore, no devaluations are currently forecast.</p>
